FILES, MECHANISMS AND ACCEPTANCE EVIDENCE
- model.rs retains the pure Envelope -> ItemId transcript projection, completion
  overwrite, pre-completion snapshot repair, generation/order ledger and reset/
  lag handling. Protocol fixture/property tests run in the GUI gate.
- bridge.rs subscribes on bbt-rt, prepares/publishes immutable snapshots off UI
  through Latest/UiSender/DirtySource and loads entire completed terminal blobs.
  The UI never awaits; the GUI disallowed-method lint passes.
- rich.rs uses bbt-doc StreamingMarkdown.append, actual reparsed_range accounting,
  syntax highlighting and retained block layouts on bounded blocking workers.
  Completed unchanged rows are reused. Structured 64KiB test: 69315 parsed bytes,
  all 64 batches appended, zero credit deferrals, 1346 prepared block layouts.
  The separate unfinished-paragraph case proves the <=4x parse-credit bound;
  deferred bytes are intentionally literal previews, formatted on completion.
- view.rs uses inset StreamDock cards, diff views, tool cards and the approval
  atom. Source/reasoning controls are compact inline buttons. Approval choices
  are compact primary/secondary/danger with distinct fills and no empty badges.
  AgentMessage/Reasoning support rich streaming, collapse/source disclosure,
  full >64KiB readability and viewport glyph filtering, with no 4KiB cap.
- Terminal's real API witness renders TOOL role, command, Running status and
  live tail mid-stream, then every 10000-word payload plus BLOB-END on completion.
  Plan/Image/Usage/Subagent remain readable plain text as assigned.
- editor.rs provides first-line history and / plus @ hooks, offering slash
  commands only. A stale completion cannot replace new typing. window.rs routes
  the same key function used by native App::key in unattended tests: approval
  Escape, completion dismissal and running-turn interruption. Ctrl-C remains a
  control-lane interrupt. Rendered approval actions send actual ResolveApproval.
- The same-store crash/reopen witness sends old-gateway Close and an old rendered
  Stop after a new attachment. Action::StopAt captures the epoch and refuses a
  replacement birth; the new actor completes another turn. No disjoint roots.
- gui_budget drives the REAL Bridge::drain_with_clock: stop at 300us, defer with
  a wake, lose nothing, preserve completed layouts. The >64KiB production replay
  test checks actual MarkdownPrepare permit calls and explicitly catches the
  registered-UI-thread panic; it does not rely on a dead flag read.

